   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion to recommit with instructions Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 197 - 225 (Roll no. 580).",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8A000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "14:24:20",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question on the motion to recommit with instructions was ordered without objection. (consideration: CR H7078)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "14:14:51",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Lewis motion to recommit with instructions. The instructions contained in the motion seek to require the bill to be reported back to the House with an amendment to prohibit provisions of the bill from applying to any cases brought under civil rights laws or the Constitution.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36100",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "14:14:19",
   "committees": [
    {
     "name": "Judiciary Committee",
     "systemCode": "hsju00",
     "url": "https://api.congress.gov/v3/committee/house/hsju00?format=json"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Lewis moved to recommit with instructions to Judiciary. (consideration: CR H7077-7078; text: CR H7077)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "14:14:06",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule. (consideration: CR H7077)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "13:11:22",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H.R. 2655.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "13:11:15",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The resolution provides for the consideration of H.R. 2655 and H.R. 982. In the case of H.R. 2655, the resolution provides for one hour of debate and one motion to recommit. In the case of H.R. 982, the resolution provides for one hour of general debate and makes in order only those amendments printed in the Rules Committee report. The resolution also provides for one motion to recommit the bill H.R. 982.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-14",
   "actionTime": "13:11:10",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 403. (consideration: CR H7069-7079)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "2013-11-12",
   "actionTime": "19:17:55",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 403 Reported to House. The resolution provides for the consideration of H.R. 2655 and H.R. 982. In the case of H.R. 2655, the resolution provides for one hour of debate and one motion to recommit. In the case of H.R. 982, the resolution provides for one hour of general debate and makes in order only those amendments printed in the Rules Committee report. The resolution also provides for one motion to recommit the bill H.R. 982.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
